Third-party data: General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects (GCAT)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

gcatpy reads data from the General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects (GCAT),
compiled and maintained by Jonathan McDowell.

  Source:     https://planet4589.org/space/gcat/
  Copyright:  (c) 2020-2026 Jonathan McDowell
  License:    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
              https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
              Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en

GCAT data are NOT covered by the MIT License. They remain under CC BY 4.0, and
anyone redistributing them, including data loaded or exported through gcatpy,
must comply with its attribution terms.

Required citation:

  McDowell, J., 2020: General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects,
  https://planet4589.org/space/gcat

When a specific GCAT release is used, McDowell also gives this form:

  McDowell, Jonathan C., 2020. General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects,
  Release <version>, https://planet4589.org/space/gcat

Distribution of GCAT data in this project:

  - The published gcatpy package (wheel) contains no GCAT data. Data are
    downloaded from the source above into a local, per-user cache only when
    the user explicitly requests it.
  - A small subset of GCAT records is redistributed in this repository as test
    fixtures under tests/fixtures/, under CC BY 4.0.

Modifications (CC BY 4.0, Section 3(a)(1)(B)):

  Data loaded through gcatpy are derived from GCAT and have been modified:
  files are parsed into typed tables, "-" placeholders are converted to nulls,
  and date fields are split into the raw string, a parsed timestamp, and a
  precision/uncertainty field. Test fixtures are unmodified extracts of the
  original TSV files unless their accompanying README states otherwise.

